Npgsql v9.0.3 for browser-wasm (applied by scripts/build-dotnet-runtime.mjs to a clean clone).

browser-wasm has no sockets and no TLS: NpgsqlConnector's static ALPN field (SslApplicationProtocol)
throws in its type initializer, and RawOpen dials a Socket. This adds a public NpgsqlStreamTransport.Connect
hook: when set, a physical connection is the Stream it returns (the runtime's virtual TCP), the ALPN value
is made lazily, and the buffers skip socket timeouts when there is no socket.

The socket's other consumers were checked: socket options (keepalive) are set only on the socket path,
disposal is null-safe, and cancellation opens its own connection through RawOpen. The one endpoint consumer,
NpgsqlActivitySource.Enrich (tracing), switches on the endpoint's type: under the transport the endpoint is
the runtime's loopback (an IPEndPoint), and Enrich takes a missing endpoint without throwing.

